WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.438
Help is a tool.

00:00:01.438 --> 00:00:04.313
Waiting forever for perfect help is a stall.

00:00:04.313 --> 00:00:07.547
This lesson is about asking for help without stalling.

00:00:07.547 --> 00:00:08.985
Peers, mentors, office hours.

00:00:08.985 --> 00:00:11.501
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:15.094
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.094 --> 00:00:20.485
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.485 --> 00:00:24.439
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:28.392
Stay practical: write one ask before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.712 --> 00:00:31.049
Use peers, mentors, and office hours.

00:00:31.049 --> 00:00:34.555
Ask one specific person for one specific next step.

00:00:34.555 --> 00:00:36.892
Remember the objective: write one ask.

00:00:36.892 --> 00:00:41.177
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.177 --> 00:00:45.852
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.852 --> 00:00:50.137
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.137 --> 00:00:54.811
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.811 --> 00:00:57.538
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:57.538 --> 00:00:59.096
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:59.416 --> 00:01:04.166
Write one ask now: who, what you tried, and what decision you need.

00:01:04.166 --> 00:01:06.358
Remember the objective: write one ask.

